# Detection 6: AWS Root Account Usage
# MITRE ATT&CK: T1078.004 (Valid Accounts: Cloud Accounts)
# Data Source: AWS CloudTrail (sourcetype=aws:cloudtrail)
#
# Logic: Any API call made by the AWS root user. Per AWS best practice
# and CIS AWS Foundations Benchmark, root should never be used for
# routine operations. Every event from userIdentity.type=Root is
# either a misconfiguration or an indicator of compromise.
#
# False-positive considerations: Initial account setup, support cases
# requiring root, and a small set of account-level actions that only
# root can perform (e.g., closing the account, changing the root
# email). All of these should be infrequent and pre-planned.

index=main sourcetype=aws:cloudtrail userIdentity.type=Root
| table _time, eventName, eventSource, sourceIPAddress, userAgent, awsRegion
| sort -_time